    "title": "Carroll preps for Plainfield as Chargers eye repeat title - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Glenn Marini ,\n49 minutes ago\nFORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) – The Carroll girls volleyball program is one win away from a perfect season, a 50-match winning streak, and back-to-back 4A state championships as the Chargers will face Plainfield for the 2025 state title on Saturday night at Gainbridge Fieldhouse.\nThe Chargers come into Saturday’s showdown with a 36-0 record while being ranked no. 5 in the country. Carroll has only dropped four sets all season long – with two of those coming against Westfield in a hard-fought semi-state semifinal victory last Saturday.\nCounting back to last season’s title run, the Chargers have won 49 matches in a row under coach Pandy Sinish.\nWith the IHSAA shifting the volleyball state title site to Gainbridge after years at Worthen Arena on Ball State’s campus in Muncie, Carrroll and Plainfield are scheduled to play at 7 pm Saturday following the 3A title match between Bishop Dwenger and Roncalli at 4:30 pm.\nWANE’s Josh Ayen will be in Indianapolis to cover both the Saints and the Chargers on Saturday night – tune into our coverage on the 11 pm news on Saturday!\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
